led parametrically from the key_parameters so that BASE_LENGTH, BASE_WIDTH, BASE_THICKNESS, ARM_HEIGHT, ARM_THICKNESS and HOLE_DIAMETER drive all geometry.\"],\"user_request_raw\":\"Read the following part request and formal dimension contract. Part request: 'Make an L-shaped bracket with a base 60 mm long, 40 mm wide, and 6 mm thick. The vertical arm is 40 mm tall, 40 mm wide, and 6 mm thick. Include two 5 mm diameter holes in the base, centered 10 mm from the short edges and 10 mm from the long edges.' Formal dimension contract: 'base_length = 60 mm; base_width = 40 mm; base_thickness = 6 mm; arm_height = 40 mm; arm_width = 40 mm; arm_thickness = 6 mm; hole_diameter = 5 mm; hole_center_offset_from_short_edge = 10 mm; hole_center_offset_from_long_edge = 10 mm; hole_count = 2.' Bind the contract to the build123d script you will create. State the formal claim you will verify.\",\"spec_version\":1}\nQA report: {\"cad_brief_id\":\"(coder-failure)\",\"engine_a\":{\"engine_name\":\"cadpy_analysis\",\"results\":[],\"summary\":\"\",\"warnings\":[],\"errors\":[],\"raw_json\":null},\"engine_b\":{\"engine_name\":\"check_mesh\",\"results\":[],\"summary\":\"\",\"warnings\":[],\"errors\":[\"Deterministic coder execution failed: cannot import name 'TDF_LabelSequence' from 'OCP.TDF' (/usr/local/lib/python3.11/site-packages/OCP/TDF/__init__.py)\\n\\nTraceback:\\nTraceback (most recent call last):\\n  File \\\"/opt/agent/agent/multi_agent_cad/nodes.py\\\", line 552, in _node_python_coder_deterministic\\n    from cadpy.generation import EntrySpec, run_script_generator\\n  File \\\"/opt/agent/agent/packages/cadpy/src/cadpy/generation.py\\\", line 40, in <module>\\n    from cadpy.glb import (\\n  File \\\"/opt/agent/agent/packages/cadpy/src/cadpy/glb.py\\\", line 32, in <module>\\n    from cadpy.step_scene import ColorRGBA, LoadedStepScene, OccurrenceNode, SelectorBundle, occurrence_selector_id\\n  File \\\"/opt/agent/agent/packages/cadpy/src/cadpy/step_scene.py\\\", line 32, in <modul